The analyst note states that firewall, proxy, and network logs did not show unusual activity or suspicious downloads.

Initial assessment:

This alert requires investigation because a suspicious Docker image build was detected shortly after reported brute-force activity against the same host. If the build was initiated by an unauthorized user and the resulting image contains malicious code, it could provide a way to execute tools within a container and reduce visibility into malicious activity. However, the image name alone does not establish malicious behavior. The Docker build history, image contents, authentication logs, and host telemetry must be reviewed to determine whether the activity was legitimate or malicious.

